# Party module

**Read the full memory model first:** [`.cursor/rules/docs/party-module.md`](docs/party-module.md)

This is the **canonical CRUD template** for backend feature modules. Inventory and other modules mirror these patterns.

## Golden rules

1. **Reads** use `prisma.client`; **writes** use `unitOfWork.run` only.
2. **All mutations** — audit + outbox in the same transaction (`AuditModule.PARTY`).
3. **Org-global** — no branch scoping on list/get.
4. **Two nesting patterns** (do not conflate):
   - Shared children (`roles`, `addresses`, `contacts`): `partyId` from **route param**
   - Role details (`customers`, `suppliers`, `doctors`, `employees`): `partyId` in **create body**, top-level routes
5. Role detail create calls `ensurePartyRole` + `assertUniqueBusinessCode`; restores soft-deleted row for same `partyId`.
6. **Party delete** blocked when any active child exists.

## Lifecycle (no workflows)

| Rule | Where |
|------|-------|
| Soft delete | `deletedAt`; filter `deletedAt: null` |
| Optimistic lock | `version` on update/delete; `optimisticUpdate()` |
| Default address | Clears other defaults of same `addressType` |
| Active party join | `activePartyFilter` on role-detail queries |

## Layer checklist

- **DTOs:** update requires `version`; no `partyId` in nested child create; `partyId` required in role-detail create.
- **Mappers:** one-way `to{Entity}Response()`; IDs as strings; `serializeDecimal` / `serializeDate`.
- **Services:** `assertPartyExists` for nested routes; exported services for cross-module use.
- **Permissions:** `PARTY:RESOURCE:ACTION` on every endpoint (`@RequirePermissions`).
- **Constants/enums:** [`party.constants.ts`](../backend/src/party/constants/party.constants.ts).
- **Utils:** [`party.util.ts`](../backend/src/party/utils/party.util.ts).

## Reporting

Three reports in [`party-reports.provider.ts`](../backend/src/reporting/providers/party/party-reports.provider.ts): `party.customer-list`, `party.supplier-list`, `party.customer-outstanding` (permission `REPORT_PARTY_VIEW`).

## Not implemented

E2E party tests, Angular clients, cascade delete, `ADMIN`/`OTHER` detail tables, entity-specific list-query DTOs.

